SUMMARY:Post feed post: Present perfect
DESCRIPTION:Publish on Instagram and Facebook: Feed post.\nOnly if present 
 perfect is live on spanish-quizz.es. If the release slipped\, move this ev
 ent by the same number of days.\n\nClip: present-perfect-feed.mp4 (tutoria
 l-videos/exports/activity-launch-videos.zip)\nTitle: New activity: Present
  perfect\n\nCaption:\nNew on Spanish Quizzes: the present perfect.\n\nHe h
 ablado\, has comido\, ha vivido. Use haber + the past participle for what 
 you have done.\n\n-ar verbs → -ado (hablado)\n-er and -ir verbs → -ido
  (comido\, vivido)\n\nThe irregular ones to learn: hecho\, dicho\, visto\,
  escrito\, vuelto\, abierto.\n\nTwo traps: the helper verb is always haber
 \, never tener\, and the participle never changes (ella ha comido).\n\n150
  practice sentences in Choose or Type mode\, each with an English translat
 ion and an explanation. Free\, no sign-up.\n\nPractise now at spanish-quiz
 z.es\n\nQuick check: ¿Alguna vez ___ estado en México? Answer in the com
 ments.\n\n🎵 Music: "Old School Salsa 03" by vjgalaxy from Pixabay\npixa
 bay.com/music/salsa-old-school-salsa-03-499570/\n\n#LearnSpanish #SpanishG
 rammar #PresentPerfect #PretéritoPerfecto #SpanishLessons #SpanishPractic
 e #AprenderEspañol #SpanishQuiz #LanguageLearning #StudySpanish
URL:https://spanish-quizz.es
